## Original Content
A "intervenção arqueológica promoveu escavações, que revelou estruturas não religiosas do antigo Convento de São Bento, fundado no século XVI, nas várias fases de ocupação do espaço -- dormitórios, enfermarias, áreas técnicas"

## Summary
Archaeological excavations at the new market in Viana do Castelo have uncovered non-religious structures from the 16th-century Convent of São Bento, including dormitories, infirmaries, and technical areas. These findings reveal various phases of occupation of the space. Works related to this project are set to resume in September.

## Key Points
- Archaeological intervention led to excavations that revealed non-religious structures of the ancient Convent of São Bento.
- The convent was founded in the 16th century and exhibits multiple phases of historical occupation.
- Key areas discovered include dormitories, infirmaries, and technical spaces.
- Excavations are part of ongoing construction works in the new market area, scheduled to continue in September.


